  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the assessor of the city of Troy to accept from the Sixth Avenue Baptist Church an application for exemption from real property taxes pursuant to section 420-a of the real property tax law",
    "basePrintNo": "S5879",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5879-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Troy, City of",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5879\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act authorizing the assessor of the city of Troy to accept from the\nSixth Avenue Baptist Church an application for exemption from real\nproperty taxes pursuant to section 420-a of the real property tax law\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nAllows the city of Troy's assessor to make corrections to the 2012,\n2013 and 2014 assessment rolls for applications for exemption from\nreal property taxes This act will apply to the specific applications\nto be submitted by the Sixth Avenue Baptist Church.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one authorizes the Sixth Avenue Baptist Church an application\nfor exemption from real property taxes for the 2012, 2013 and 2014\nassessment rolls If the application is received on or before the\ntaxable status dates, the church may be eligible for the 2012, 2013\nand 2014 tax refund Once approved by the Common Council of the city of\nTroy, the assessor is able to correct the subject rolls for the years\nindicated and the church shall pay the appropriate taxes and be\neligible to receive tax refunds Provided the correction is approved,\nany unpaid taxes, fines, penalties, interest or tax liens from 2012,\n2013 and 2014 will be canceled\n\nSection two provides for the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUpon request, this legislation allows the Sixth Avenue Baptist Church\nin the city of Troy to apply for a real estate tax exemption for the\nyears 2012, 2013 and 2014.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
